,title,link,text,language,family
0,Koraga language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koraga_language,"Koraga (IPA: [korɐɡɐ], also rendered Koragar, Koragara, Korangi) is a Dravidian language spoken by the Koraga people, a Scheduled tribe people of Dakshina Kannada, Karnataka, and Kerala in South West India.","Koraga, Korra",Dravidian
1,Koraga language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korra_Koraga,"January 6, 2026 - Koraga (IPA: [korɐɡɐ], also ... is a Dravidian language spoken by the Koraga people, a Scheduled tribe people of Dakshina Kannada, Karnataka, and Kerala in South West India. The dialect spoken by the Koraga tribe in Kerala, Mudu Koraga, is divergent enough to not be intelligible with Korra ...","Koraga, Korra",Dravidian
2,Koraga language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/koraga_language,"The primary regional dialects are Onti Koraga, Tappu Koraga, Mudu Koraga, and Ande Koraga. Onti Koraga is spoken primarily in Udupi district, Karnataka, with strong Tulu influences due to bilingualism among speakers.","Koraga, Korra",Dravidian
